\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{What remains after links are integrated out}
\date{2026-11-11}

\p{In the repeated-path example \ref{fdip-00MS}, both
recorded links are equal, even when the fine weight is one.
The retained distribution is then a diagonal Haar law.
For a single retained link obtained from two successive
independent Haar links, the reference is instead Haar
on the whole group, by \ref{fdip-00MR}. An additional
fine weight changes the density relative to that reference
by \ref{fdip-00MQ}. What data must accompany the density
so that another integration step recovers the same
observable integrals?}
